  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 359 AM MDT THU OCT 8 2026\nThe upper low will progress south across Oregon and into \nnorthern California on Sunday. The low will transport hurricane\nremnants originating from the eastern Pacific to the north. The\nbulk of this moisture is expected to remain south and east of \nour area, but is likely to clip south-central Idaho, including \nthe Magic Valley, with significant rainfall possible Sunday and\nMonday. Confidence in significant precipitation amounts \nis lower to the west and north, but may also develop over the \nsouthwest Idaho highlands and central Idaho mountains. Snow \nlevels will remain above 7000 to 8000 feet due to the tropical \norigin of the moisture. Instability will be very limited, but \nany embedded thunderstorms could produce heavy rainfall. In \naddition to the moisture, the low will also usher in cooler air,\nwith highs dropping a few more degrees, except 10 to 15 degrees\ncooler across south-central Idaho where rain will hold \ntemperatures down further. Highs will be around 10 degrees below\nnormal, and lows in the agricultural valleys will dip into the\n30s with frost possible especially if skies clear. Winds will \nremain breezy on Sunday, then taper off Monday.\n\nThe low will gradually move east on Tuesday, but how far south\nit travels before moving east will determine how much moisture\nwraps around into our area. For now, this results in a 20 to 40%\nchance of precipitation, highest across southern and central \nIdaho. Temperatures will rebound slightly, but remain below \nnormal. Ensembles have come into better agreement that a Pacific\ntrough will move across our area on Wednesday and exit the area\nThursday. Rain and snow in this pattern will favor the west- \ncentral Idaho and Boise mountains, with light snow accumulations\npossible above 6000 to 7000 feet. This trough will also bring \nbreezy conditions back to the area with continued cool \ntemperatures. Precipitation should taper off by Thursday as an \nupper level ridge builds along the coast.",
